# NOTE: Do NOT add `shrinkwrap=false` here.
# It is not a valid npm config (npm warns to use --package-lock) and it breaks
# resolution of `$`-referenced entries in package.json "overrides" (e.g. `"ws": "$ws"`),
# causing `npm install` to fail with: "Unable to resolve reference $ws".
#
# Root-level "overrides" already take precedence over a dependency's bundled
# npm-shrinkwrap.json for the top-level tree, so no npm config is needed for that.
# (Some deeply-nested, shrinkwrapped subtrees — e.g. @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent —
# are not reached by root overrides; that is a separate security concern, tracked outside
# this file, not something the removed `shrinkwrap` setting ever actually fixed.)
